<step1>
<ptxt>DTC Combination Table (V Bus Branch Line Open, Past Communication Stop Malfunction)</ptxt>
<step2>
<ptxt>For past malfunctions of ECUs connected to the V bus (displayed normally in the CAN bus connected ECU check but a DTC is output), refer to the combination table to determine the branch line in which the malfunction occurred.</ptxt>
<atten4>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>ECUs with a branch line open circuit or communication stop cannot respond to the DTC output request from the SST (TaSCAN).</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>A current branch line open circuit or communication stop can be confirmed by performing the "CAN Bus Connected ECU Check" using the SST (TaSCAN): the ECUs and sensors connected to the open branch line do not respond (are not displayed on the screen).</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>If the CAN gateway ECU is outputting a malfunction code, inspect and repair the V bus No.2 malfunction first.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten4>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="C219745" width="7.106578999in" height="7.795582503in"/>
</figure>
<atten4>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>×: May be output when there is a one-side open circuit in a branch line</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>*1: DTCs cannot be output while communication is stopped</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>*2:CAN: Applies when the gateway ECU DTCs are normal (V bus No.2 normal)</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten4>
